work or from photographs. TIREKICK did not query any title registry - this is a reading of your own paperwork, and paperwork can be incomplete or forged. Confirm the brand with your state&#x27;s motor vehicle agency before you buy, and price the car as branded until you have.</div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:13px">Ask an independent mechanic to inspect this on a lift before you buy. TIREKICK cannot assess it from photos, video, or audio.</div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Vehicle record</div><div class="panel"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr));gap:16px"><div><div class="mono-label">VIN</div><div>1HGCR2F37DA******</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Year</div><div>2013</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Make</div><div>HONDA</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Model</div><div>Accord</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Trim</div><div>LX</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Engine</div><div>2.4L 4-cyl K24W1</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Drive</div><div>-</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Body</div><div>Sedan/Saloon</div></div></div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:16px">VIN is 17 characters and passes its position-9 check digit, so it is internally consistent. That confirms the number was transcribed correctly. It does not confirm the number belongs to the car in the photographs.</div><div style="margin-top:20px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--tk-line)"><div class="mono-label" style="color:var(--tk-locked)">Recalls - what this list is</div><div class="prose" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:8px;color:var(--tk-locked)">5 recall campaign(s) on record for the 2013 HONDA Accord. NHTSA publishes recalls by model, not by VIN, and does not publish whether a campaign was carried out on any individual vehicle. So this is a list of what could apply to this car - not a list of what is outstanding on it. A dealer can tell you, by VIN, in a phone call, and the work is free.</div></div><div style="margin-top:20px"><div class="mono-label">Owner complaints for this model</div><div style="display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:10px"><div><div style="font-size:26px">1,418</div><div class="muted" style="font-size:11px">complaints filed</div></div><div style="flex:1 1 320px"><table style="margin-top:0"><tbody><tr><td style="font-size:12px">STEERING</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">497</td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:12px">ELECTRICAL SYSTEM</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">413</td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:12px">ENGINE</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">179</td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:12px">UNKNOWN OR OTHER</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">118</td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:12px">SERVICE BRAKES</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">115</td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:12px">POWER TRAIN</td><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px;text-align:right;width:70px">109</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:12px">Complaints filed with NHTSA by owners of the 2013 HONDA Accord, across the whole model year. They describe the model. None of them describes this car, and a high count on a common vehicle is partly just a high count of vehicles.</div></div><div style="margin-top:20px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--tk-line)"><div class="mono-label">Sources</div><ul style="margin:10px 0 0;padding-left:18px;font-size:12px"><li class="muted" style="margin-bottom:8px"><span style="color:var(--tk-text)">NHTSA vPIC</span> <span style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span><div style="margin-top:2px">What the manufacturer encoded into this VIN. It describes how the vehicle left the factory, not its condition today.</div></li><li class="muted" style="margin-bottom:8px"><span style="color:var(--tk-text)">NHTSA Safety Recalls</span> <span style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:29Z)</span><div style="margin-top:2px">Every safety recall campaign NHTSA has filed against the 2013 HONDA Accord. Keyed to the model, not to this VIN.</div></li><li class="muted" style="margin-bottom:8px"><span style="color:var(--tk-text)">NHTSA Owner Complaints</span> <span style="color:var(--tk-unknown)">(retrieved 2026-07-26T23:31:36Z)</span><div style="margin-top:2px">Owner-filed complaint counts for the 2013 HONDA ACCORD. Counts only - the narratives belong to the people who wrote them and are not retained.</div></li></ul></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Price check</div><div class="panel"><div style="display:flex;gap:32px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline"><div><div class="mono-label">Asking</div><div style="font-size:30px">$8,900</div></div><div><div class="mono-label">Supported by these comps</div><div style="font-size:30px;color:var(--tk-accent)">$6,928 - $7,568</div></div></div><div class="prose" style="font-size:14px;margin-top:16px">The asking price of $8,900 is above the $6,928-$7,568 range these comparable listings support after the deductions above. The gap is $1,332.</div><div style="margin-top:20px"><div class="mono-label">The comps behind this range</div><table style="margin-top:8px"><thead><tr><th>Listing</th><th>Year / trim</th><th>Mileage</th><th>Asking</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year, LX trim</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>112,300</td><td>$9,400</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - local listing, same model year</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>134,800</td><td>$8,100</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - listing 40 miles away, lower mileage</td><td>2013 EX</td><td>98,500</td><td>$10,200</td></tr><tr><td class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Pasted by the buyer - high-mileage example, same trim</td><td>2013 LX</td><td>151,000</td><td>$7,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style="margin-top:20px"><div class="mono-label">Deductions, each linked to a finding</div><table style="margin-top:8px"><tbody><tr><td><a href="#vf_rust_01">Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</a></td><td style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">-$600 to -$900</td><td class="muted prose" style="font-size:12px">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.72.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="#vf_tire_01">Front left tread appears low</a></td><td style="color:var(--tk-sev-major);white-space:nowrap">-$380 to -$620</td><td class="muted prose" style="font-size:12px">Repair cost band attached to this finding. Confidence in the finding itself is 0.58.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:18px">Mileage adjustment of $-0.056 per mile, fitted from the 4 comparable listings provided rather than from any assumed depreciation rate. Range built from 4 listing(s) you provided. It reflects those listings and nothing else - not a market index, not an appraisal. Asking prices, not sale prices. What a car is listed at and what it sells for are different numbers, and the second one is not public. Subject mileage of 128,540 is as stated by the seller and has not been verified.</div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Questions for the seller</div><ol class="prose" style="padding-left:22px;font-size:14px"><li style="margin-bottom:8px">How long has the rust on the rocker panel been there, and has any bodywork been done to it?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Do you know how the dent on the rear quarter happened?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">The check-engine light is on in your photo. What code is it throwing, and how long has it been on?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Can you show me the title and any service records so I can check the mileage history?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">How old are the tires, and were they all replaced at the same time?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Is the engine losing any fluid? When were the fluids last topped up or changed?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Recall 25V422000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Recall 23V858000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Recall 20V769000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Recall 17V418000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Recall 13V297000 covers this model year. Has it been done on this car, and do you have the dealer paperwork?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Owners of this model most often report problems with steering. Has this car had any work done there?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">My paperwork mentions hail damage. Can you walk me through what happened, and show me the title itself?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Do you have service records? Can I see them before I come out?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Has this car been in any accident, reported or not?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Are you the titleholder, and is the title in hand and clear?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Can I take it to my mechanic for a pre-purchase inspection?</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px">Has any recall work been done on this car? A dealer will check by VIN and do outstanding recall work free - can you show me the paperwork?</li></ol></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Negotiation script</div><div style="display:grid;gap:12px"><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Open by naming what you did</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I ran the photos and the VIN through an AI analysis before coming out. It flagged a few things I want to look at with you.”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Raise: Corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis flagged corrosion visible along driver-side rocker panel. I&#x27;d want that looked at - a shop quoted that kind of work at roughly $600 to $900. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Raise: Front left tread appears low</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis flagged front left tread appears low. I&#x27;d want that looked at - a shop quoted that kind of work at roughly $380 to $620. Can we talk about the price with that in mind?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Anchor on the comps</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I looked at comparable listings and they support roughly $6,928 to $7,568 for this car in this condition. Here are the listings I looked at. Can you meet me in that range?”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Protect yourself on what the analysis could not see</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“The analysis was clear that it can&#x27;t assess brakes, airbags, frame, or steering from photos. I&#x27;d like to take it to my mechanic before we finalize. If that&#x27;s not possible, I understand, but then I&#x27;d need the price to reflect the risk I&#x27;m taking on.”</div></div><div class="panel"><div class="mono-label">Be willing to leave</div><div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:14px">“I appreciate your time. Let me think it over and I&#x27;ll call you tomorrow.”</div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="section-label">Run metadata</div><table><tbody><tr><td class="mono-label">Mode</td><td>fixture</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Images analyzed</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Tokens</td><td>0 in / 0 out</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Audio processed</td><td>22.0s</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Cost to produce</td><td style="color:var(--tk-accent)">$0.0000</td></tr><tr><td class="mono-label">Note</td><td class="prose muted" style="font-size:12px">Fixture mode: responses served from cache, no API calls billed. $0.00 is the true cost of this run and not a placeholder.</td></tr></tbody></table></section><footer style="margin-top:72px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--tk-line);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:11px"><span class="mono-label">INSPECTED BY TIREKICK AI</span><span class="muted prose" style="max-width:620px">Automated analysis of buyer-supplied media. Not an inspection. Have an independent mechanic examine any vehicle before you buy it. <a href="/accuracy">Accuracy and known limits</a>.</span></footer></div>"`;
